{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/zwnovh","slide":4,"text":"agent.html declares the authenticated and signed-out regions, upload form, progress, analysis cards, and empty state. agent.js sits between those visible regions and external services. It receives DOM events, updates the page, obtains the current Firebase ID token, and sends authenticated Agent API requests. Video functions also reserve sessions, transfer chunks, inspect progress, and recover. agent.css is page-specific while base.css provides shared styling primitives."}
