{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ku9v5e","slide":5,"text":"The HTML loads Firebase Auth before agent.js. start() observes onAuthStateChanged(). Before a protected request, authorized() gets the current user's ID token and sets the Authorization header. Hosting forwards the relative route to the API. The API verifies identity, custom claims, and ownership. request() parses the normal response envelope. Server failures retain a safe requestId for diagnosis."}
